Reactor Effect Client

This independent SDK is not an official Reactor SDK. The repository is a Bun
workspace publishing three packages; each package ships its own NOTICE and the
third-party texts under its notices/ directory.

The canonical wire definitions and selected protocol behavior derive from:
- reactor-client-sdks, commit 24f1865b48f03354b15402731f1b92e90ceee92a
- reactor-runtime, commit 8e98536c6daedca298700dc45cbb5fd9e3676f16
Their upstream licenses and notices are retained under packages/client/notices/.
packages/client/wire/proto contains the selected canonical protocol sources.
The generated wire module also incorporates Google's protobuf Struct
descriptor; see packages/client/notices/google-protobuf-LICENSE.

Session, correlation, observation and browser-media implementations incorporate
the user-supplied reactor-effect-client reference source. Reusable H3, coordinator,
reference and engine behavior is extracted from the user's the-show source.
The extracted packages do not depend on the-show or ship its application policy.

The native transport is built from the Rust bridge in packages/native/rust against:
reactor-webrtc, commit bebf63e42624ee440e066b692494dd3229d29ae7 (Apache-2.0).
It incorporates upstream Google WebRTC binaries and associated third-party code.
The pinned reactor-webrtc Apache terms are retained in
packages/native/notices/reactor-webrtc-LICENSE. Exact macOS arm64 and Linux x64
prebuilt SBOMs, plus the pinned WebRTC BSD license and patent grant, are
retained under packages/native/notices/reactor-webrtc/. Component-specific
third-party redistribution texts for every component named by those SBOMs are
retained under packages/native/notices/reactor-webrtc/third-party/; its README
names the exact pinned source revision and retained license/copyright or patent
file for each component. The Rust crates linked into the native bridge and
their selected license texts are recorded under
packages/native/notices/native-rust/.
Native builds pin and verify the upstream binary artifact checksum.
No reactor-ffi or reactor-core session implementation is included.

Effect is MIT-licensed. Every package declares Effect as a peer dependency; its
license is retained in each package's notices/effect-LICENSE. Koffi is an
optional dependency of reactor-effect-native only; its installed distribution
retains its upstream license. Development tooling and node_modules are excluded
from the npm packages.

The reference archive's limited TypeScript WebRTC/codec implementation is not
part of any package's production graph. Retained owned-webrtc notices under
packages/client/notices/ document the supplied reference and vector provenance;
they do not indicate that a second WebRTC engine is shipped or supported.
